  "reason": "Complete construction and prerequisite audit; see research/phase-2-next-20-batch-4.notes.md and coverage.json. Source D, §4.5 opening p.240 and Theorem 4.4.8 pp.237–238; documented alternative-proof disposition, no raw fetch claim. Put D_n=M_n-M_{n-1}. It is in L2 by (a-b)^2<=2a^2+2b^2, and E[D_n|F_{n-1}]=0 by the differences theorem. Cauchy–Schwarz makes M_{n-1}D_n L1, so the unbounded taking-out theorem gives E[M_{n-1}D_n|F_{n-1}]=0. Expand M_n^2-M_{n-1}^2=2M_{n-1}D_n+D_n^2 and condition. Subtraction of Delta<M>_n=E[D_n^2|F_{n-1}] yields zero conditional drift. The square and bracket terms are adapted L1. For the centered assertion N_n=M_n-M_0 is a square-integrable martingale because M_0 is measurable for every F_n; N_0=0 and Delta N_n=D_n, hence <N>=<M>. Apply the same proved calculation to N. This proves both statements, without inferring one by subtracting an unjustified product martingale. AC is inherited from the Radon–Nikodym construction of conditional expectation; if a sequence of versions is needed, AC selects measurable versions at the countably many times. Identities remain identities of almost-sure classes, without completing the filtration.",
